From: apklayer
Subject: [PATCH] libhwbinder: a host hwbinder context (Waydroid's host_hwbinder) for device HALs

apklayer patch (docs/PATCHES.md, docs/HALIUM.md). As libbinder's (frameworks/native 0006) for HIDL: a second ProcessState on
/dev/host_hwbinder (apklayer's path layer maps it to $APKLAYER_HOST_HWBINDER: a Halium device's own /dev/hwbinder, or another
instance's hwbinder in the two-instance test), IPCThreadState::self(true) with its own TLS key and thread pool (started without
waiting for a local hwservicemanager), BpHwBinder remembers its context, Parcels received through it (by buffer address) or
carrying its proxies (64-bit: a flag in padding; 32-bit has none) use it, buffers are freed through it, a host proxy's handle entry is expunged from the host context. Also Waydroid libhwbinder
0002: no FLAT_BINDER_FLAG_TXN_SECURITY_CTX on our binders (no kernel security context here; libbinder's is our frameworks/native
0001). Ported from Waydroid's libhwbinder 0001 (Android 13), which switched one ProcessState between the two drivers instead.
ABI kept: Parcel's size is unchanged, BpHwBinder/ProcessState/IPCThreadState are only made by libhwbinder. Rebuild: `m libhidlbase`.
Against system/libhwbinder 2f5282448223 (REVISION). Apply: patches/apply aosp <LineageOS tree>.
